se you don't  understand  i remember with you know my wife who  speaks some spanish a fair amount of  french we were in portugal she has some  familiarity with portuguese but being  there had no impact on her at all  in terms of improving her portuguese and  even with me  i remember i went once after having done  a little bit of work with this was  before we had portuguese at length some  living language material that i had gone  through and i went to portugal like i  couldn't even get started because i  didn't understand what people were  saying but then after working at  portuguese  uh at link and and listening to a lot of  our in the podcast especially the the  radio  rtf podcasts out of  portuguese radio then when i went there  and i had a sufficient grass then the  experience became dense it became  intense and so that's why i think  that by going there now i think i have  sufficient i have a sufficient  background in check that i have a chance  now of course a lot will depend on how  intense a language experience i can  create for myself in prague so i have  lined up twice a day lessons with  tutors teachers where we basically talk  like i'm doing now via skype  through link and i get a report after  the discussion with my mistakes which i  then review and so forth and so on  because i want to make sure that i get  enough opportunity to speak the language  i don't want to wander around the city  hoping that i bump into someone who's  willing to talk to me  what other adventures i'm going to find  there i don't know we're going to have  our meet up the first night  maybe i'll i'll if all the pubs in the  center of the city are full of  foreigners i'll take a bus and go  uh you know to the outskirts and try to  find a pub where checks are discussing  the latest corruption scandal  yeah in the czech republic and i'll  chime in with my two cents worth and  maybe get a conversation that way i will  see it's going to be a mystery to me but  i'm hoping that i can create an intense  uh  language experience an immersion an  intense involvement with the language  that's going to catapult my largely  passive knowledge of the language into  active knowledge so  what are we today the 17th or so  uh we're basically  two weeks away  so uh i'm very much very much looking  forward to  my five days to fluency in prague we  will see what happens thank you for  listening
 

